[17592186354279 #edb/ref 1069 "q-84020" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354279 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354279 #edb/ref 1071 "The number of heads facing upward after tossing $2$ unfair coins follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the number of heads facing upward after tossing the $2$ coins?\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354279 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e4d143c-c13b-5ae0-a77b-3da97ad8ff9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354279 #edb/ref 1074 "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{9})+1(\\frac{4}{9})+2(\\frac{4}{9}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355049 #edb/ref 1080 "1.5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355049 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355049 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2caf601c-b68b-5641-9bcb-7727613b6286" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356220 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356220 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356220 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b09bb1f2-5bf8-596e-9a70-aa6dafe756fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356408 #edb/ref 1080 "2.5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356408 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356408 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c7862014-d396-52a6-aec9-f81ecf2bc212" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356627 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218