f(-2)=f(-1)=f(1)=f(3)=f(5)=f(6)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-2)\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+1\\cdot f(1)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =(-2)(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6})+6(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{6}+\\frac{-1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-1+1+3+5+6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370946 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186370947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370946 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370946 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370946 #edb/ref 1071 "A bag contains $4$ five-dollar bills, $8$ ten-dollar bills, and $6$ twenty-dollar bills. If one bill is randomly drawn from a bag, what is its expected value?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370946 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3b33e7f8-97bd-52b2-9fc5-eb73c2b2d7ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370946 #edb/ref 1074 "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value of a randomly drawn bill. Then the support is $S={5,10,20}.$\n\nIn the bag there are  $4$ five-dollar bills, $8$ ten-dollar bills and $6$ twenty-dollar bills (eighteen bills in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5) & =\\frac{4}{18}=\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{8}{18}=\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ P(20) & =\\frac{6}{18}=\\frac{3}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =5\\cdot f(5)+10\\cdot f(10)+20\\cdot f(20) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{2}{9})+10(\\frac{4}{9})+20(\\frac{3}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}+\\frac{40}{9}+\\frac{60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+40+60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370947 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370947 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370947 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370947 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370947 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370947 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370947 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370947 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186370951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370947 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "45d39d50-e814-58b3-b920-cbbb549d00fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370948 #edb/ref 1080 "20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370948 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370948 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28ce0594-ae9a-5533-b4e8-9b16a4434e24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370949 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{70}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370949 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370949 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dc2d678f-d252-5400-be5e-828422888057" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370950 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370950 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370950 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "39a17018-6a1b-5fa0-a4b2-d57693172562" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370951 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{110}{9}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370951 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370951 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b8d0e30-5870-5882-90fe-bbe6d3d8ae98" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370952 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370952 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370952 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11bce5a2-21ae-5099-b